# Wave G.b — Per-package HTTP handler load

## Problem

Hostile audit blocker #5: `loadWorkspaceHttpPackageHandlers()` (codegen) **eagerly** `await import`s every product HTTP package (denali host http, finance-http, guest-club, urban) on first call. `apps/api/src/app.ts` awaits that bag before `tryDispatchWorkspaceRoutes`, so the first workspace HTTP request pays multi-product fan-in even when only one package’s route matched.

Wave C/G.a improved transpile **lists**; they do not fix this **runtime** eager load.

## Decision

1. Codegen emits **per-package** loaders plus a handler→package map:

| Export | Role |
| ------ | ---- |
| `loadWorkspaceHttpHandlersForPackage(pkg)` | Dynamic `import()` **one** handler package |
| `ensureWorkspaceHttpHandler(key)` | Resolve one handler via per-package cache |
| `resetWorkspaceHttpHandlerPackageCache()` | Test reset |
| `loadWorkspaceHttpPackageHandlers()` | **Compat** — loads all packages (tests / ownership proofs only) |

2. Hot path (`app.ts` → registrar) uses `ensureWorkspaceHttpHandler` after route match — **not** the all-packages loader.
3. `tryDispatchWorkspaceRoutes` takes `resolveHandler(key) => Promise<fn>` instead of a preloaded `WorkspaceRouteHandlers` bag.
4. Guards (`guard-api-lazy-plugin-registry`, `guard-guest-api-shell`) require the per-package ensure API on the boot path and forbid `app.ts` calling `loadWorkspaceHttpPackageHandlers`.

## Out of scope

- Removing `loadWorkspaceHttpPackageHandlers` entirely (finance ownership specs still assert import sites in the generated file)
- Marketplace / remote plugin discovery
- Changing route path inventory or `HANDLER_DISPATCH_KIND`

## Verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm run guard:workspace-registry-fresh
node scripts/guards/guard-api-lazy-plugin-registry.mjs
node scripts/guards/guard-guest-api-shell.mjs
node --test scripts/test/http-handler-per-package-load.spec.mjs
pnpm --filter @apps/api exec node --import tsx --test \
  src/workspace-finance/finance-http-handlers-ownership.spec.ts
```
